<title>USA: Lexmark sees Q1 revs below estimates.</title>
<headline>Lexmark sees Q1 revs below estimates.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Ky. 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lexmark International Group Inc said on Wednesday it expects first-quarter revenues to be lower than analysts' estimates but said operating income and net income would meet Wall Street's expectations.</p>
<p>Lexmark said quarterly revenues would grow from the $588 million reported a year ago but not as much as analysts' forecasts, due to price reductions, unfavorable translation of foreign revenues and the company's exit from the keyboard business.</p>
<p>First quarter results are scheduled for release April 21.</p>
<p>Lexmark makes printers and related products.</p>
</text>
